 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
 
+## Board Publications
+
+### `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Publishes the board, allowing anyone with its secret public URL to view it without signing in. Only account admins (including owners) with access to the board can publish it; other members, including board creators, receive `403 Forbidden`.
+
+No request body is required. Returns `200 OK` with the board JSON, including its `public_url`. Repeated requests preserve the existing URL.
+
+### `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Unpublishes the board and revokes its public URL, including direct links to its columns and cards. Requires the same permissions as publishing. Returns `204 No Content`, including if the board is already unpublished. The board's `public_url` becomes `null`. Publishing it again generates a new secret URL.
+
+### Public pages
+
+These read-only HTML pages require no authentication or account prefix:
+
+- `GET /public/boards/:key` — the published board and its published cards.
+- `GET /public/boards/:key/columns/:id` — a column belonging to that board.
+- `GET /public/boards/:key/cards/:number` — a published card belonging to that board.
+
+Invalid or revoked keys, draft cards, and columns or cards outside the board return `404 Not Found`. Publishing does not change signed-in board membership or grant editing access.
+
 ## Board Accesses
 
+
 Board accesses let you see who has access to a board and their involvement level (watching or access only). Any board member can view this information.
 
 ### `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/accesses`
